---
import ServiceLayout from '../../layouts/ServiceLayout.astro';
import FAQSchema from '../../components/FAQSchema.astro';
import { serviceFAQs } from '../../data/serviceFAQs';
import { getService } from '../../data/services';
import { business } from '../../data/business';

const service = getService('balayage');

const pageTitle = "Balayage North Auckland, $280, 3–4 Hours";
const pageDescription = "Balayage in Kaukapakapa, North Auckland for $280. Hand-painted, low-maintenance colour with Melissa, 3 to 4 hours. Near Helensville and Kumeū. Book online.";
const pageKeywords = "balayage north auckland, balayage kaukapakapa, balayage helensville, balayage kumeu, hand painted highlights, balayage cost, balayage price nz";

const faqs = serviceFAQs['balayage'];
---

<ServiceLayout
  title={pageTitle}
  description={pageDescription}
  keywords={pageKeywords}
  price={service.price}
  duration={service.duration}
  h1={service.h1}
  serviceName={service.name}
  image="/images/services/balayage-hero-1200.webp"
  imageSrcset="/images/services/balayage-hero-640.webp 640w, /images/services/balayage-hero-1200.webp 1200w, /images/services/balayage-hero-1600.webp 1600w"
  imageSizes="100vw"
  imageWidth={1600}
  imageHeight={893}
  imageAlt="Illustration: a hairdresser hand-painting balayage onto long brunette hair"
  ogImage="https://hairbymelissa.co.nz/images/services/balayage-hero-og.jpg"
  showCta={false}
>
  <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6">
    Balayage is hand-painted colour that looks natural and grows out softly, with no hard regrowth line. At Hair By Melissa in Kaukapakapa, North Auckland, it's $280 and takes 3 to 4 hours, one-on-one with Melissa. It's a short drive from Helensville, Waitoki and Wainui, and about 25 minutes up SH16 from Kumeū.
  </p>

  <dl class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 bg-[#F8F9FA] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
    <div>
      <dt class="text-sm uppercase text-gray-600">Price</dt>
      <dd class="font-semibold text-salon-darkblue">$280</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt class="text-sm uppercase text-gray-600">Time</dt>
      <dd class="font-semibold text-salon-darkblue">3 to 4 hours</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt class="text-sm uppercase text-gray-600">Refresh</dt>
      <dd class="font-semibold text-salon-darkblue">8 to 12 weeks, or longer</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt class="text-sm uppercase text-gray-600">Open</dt>
      <dd class="font-semibold text-salon-darkblue">7 days</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>

  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 mb-10">
    <a href="/booking/" class="btn-primary inline-flex items-center justify-center">Book balayage</a>
    <a href={business.phoneHref} class="bg-transparent border-2 border-gray-900 text-gray-900 font-medium py-3 px-6 rounded-md hover:bg-gray-900 hover:text-white transition duration-300 ease-in-out inline-flex items-center justify-center">Call {business.phoneDisplay}</a>
  </div>

  <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">What is balayage?</h2>
  <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
    Balayage comes from the French word for "to sweep". Instead of sectioning your hair into foils, Melissa paints the colour on by hand, placing it where the light would naturally catch your hair. The result is soft and dimensional, and it can be as subtle or as bright as you like.
  </p>
  <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
    Because there's no solid line of colour at the root, it grows out gently. That's the main reason people choose it over foils, especially if getting to the salon every six weeks doesn't suit your life.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">Real balayage results</h2>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-3">
    <img
      src="/images/transformations/balayage-brunette-lob-800.webp"
      srcset="/images/transformations/balayage-brunette-lob-480.webp 480w, /images/transformations/balayage-brunette-lob-800.webp 800w"
      sizes="(min-width: 640px) 50vw, 100vw"
      alt="Before and after: shoulder-length brunette hair with soft caramel balayage"
      width="800"
      height="1000"
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async"
      class="w-full h-auto rounded-lg"
    />
    <img
      src="/images/transformations/blonde-balayage-refresh-800.webp"
      srcset="/images/transformations/blonde-balayage-refresh-480.webp 480w, /images/transformations/blonde-balayage-refresh-800.webp 800w"
      sizes="(min-width: 640px) 50vw, 100vw"
      alt="Before and after: long blonde hair refreshed with brighter, blended balayage"
      width="800"
      height="1000"
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async"
      class="w-full h-auto rounded-lg"
    />
  </div>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-8">Melissa's clients. See more in the <a href="/gallery/" class="text-salon-darkblue underline hover:text-[#0F7A9C]">gallery</a>.</p>

  <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">How much does balayage cost?</h2>
  <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
    Balayage at Hair By Melissa is <strong>$280</strong>. Longer or thicker hair can take more time to process and style, so Melissa will confirm your appointment time at your consultation. For how that compares around the country, read <a href="/blog/balayage-cost-nz/" class="text-salon-darkblue underline hover:text-[#0F7A9C]">how much balayage costs in NZ</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">What happens at your appointment</h2>
  <ol class="list-decimal list-inside text-gray-700 mb-6 space-y-2">
    <li>A chat about the look you want and what suits your hair</li>
    <li>Colour mixed for your shade</li>
    <li>Lightener painted on by hand, section by section</li>
    <li>Processing time for soft transitions</li>
    <li>Toning to get the warmth or coolness right</li>
    <li>Finish and styling, so you can see the result properly</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
    It's one client at a time, so nobody is waiting for your chair. Bring a book. Three to four hours goes quicker than you'd think.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">Who does balayage suit?</h2>
  <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-700 mb-6 space-y-2">
    <li><strong>Brunettes:</strong> caramel, honey and golden tones add warmth</li>
    <li><strong>Blondes:</strong> soft, bright pieces without a heavy root line</li>
    <li><strong>Darker hair:</strong> lighter brown tones that look sun-lightened</li>
    <li><strong>Curly hair:</strong> colour that follows your natural movement</li>
    <li><strong>Busy people:</strong> fewer trips to the salon</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
    Want brighter, more even colour from root to tip? A <a href="/services/full-head-highlights/" class="text-salon-darkblue underline hover:text-[#0F7A9C]">full head of foils</a> may suit you better. The <a href="/blog/balayage-vs-highlights/" class="text-salon-darkblue underline hover:text-[#0F7A9C]">balayage vs highlights guide</a> compares the two.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">How long does balayage last?</h2>
  <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
    There's no fixed date. Balayage grows out softly over several months, so you can come back when you feel ready. If you like to keep the contrast fresh, plan on every 8 to 12 weeks. A <a href="/services/toner/" class="text-salon-darkblue underline hover:text-[#0F7A9C]">toner</a> between visits is a quick way to freshen your shade.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">Looking after your balayage</h2>
  <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-700 mb-6 space-y-2">
    <li>Use a colour-safe, sulfate-free shampoo and conditioner</li>
    <li>Use purple shampoo weekly if you have blonde tones</li>
    <li>Protect your hair from sun and chlorine, especially over summer</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
    The <a href="/blog/hair-color-maintenance/" class="text-salon-darkblue underline hover:text-[#0F7A9C]">colour maintenance guide</a> has more, and a <a href="/services/uv-protection-treatments/" class="text-salon-darkblue underline hover:text-[#0F7A9C]">UV protection treatment</a> is a good add-on before summer.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-6">Coming from Helensville or Kumeū?</h2>
  <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
    Hair By Melissa is at 12 Magnolia Lane, Kaukapakapa, about 15 minutes from <a href="/locations/helensville/" class="text-salon-darkblue underline hover:text-[#0F7A9C]">Helensville</a> and about 25 minutes from <a href="/locations/kumeu/" class="text-salon-darkblue underline hover:text-[#0F7A9C]">Kumeū</a>. Parking is free at the door. Balayage takes a good chunk of the day, and Melissa is open Sundays from 9am to 5pm if a weekend suits you better.
  </p>

  <div class="bg-[#F8F9FA] rounded-lg p-6 mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Ready to book?</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">$280, 3 to 4 hours, one-on-one with Melissa. Book online any time or call {business.phoneDisplay}.</p>
    <a href="/booking/" class="btn-primary inline-flex items-center justify-center">Book balayage</a>
  </div>

  <!-- FAQ Schema -->
  <Fragment slot="after">
    <FAQSchema
      faqs={faqs}
      pageUrl="https://hairbymelissa.co.nz/services/balayage/"
    />
  </Fragment>
</ServiceLayout>
